course: french
lesson: 11
title: Dates and birthdays
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A French date is a little recipe: le, then the number, then the month, so the 14th of October is le quatorze octobre.
explain: Only the first day of a month is special: it is le premier mai (the first of May), but after that just plain numbers, le deux mai, le trois mai.
explain: France writes dates day first, like the UK, so 05/03 is the 5th of March; an American reading it as May 3rd would send a birthday card two months late.
explain: At a French birthday party the tune is the same as "Happy birthday", but the words are Joyeux anniversaire, and someone shouts Souffle les bougies ! (blow out the candles!).
explain: French years are said as one big number: 2026 is deux mille vingt-six, "two thousand twenty-six", never "twenty twenty-six".
fact: The first of a month is le premier (written le 1er): le premier mai; every other date uses a plain number: le deux mai, le douze juin.
fact: France writes dates day/month/year, like the UK; in the US the month comes first, so 05/03 means 5 March in France but May 3rd in the US.
fact: C'est quand, ton anniversaire ? means "When is your birthday?" to a friend; to a grown-up it is C'est quand, votre anniversaire ?
fact: The answer pattern is Mon anniversaire, c'est le + number + month: Mon anniversaire, c'est le douze juin.
fact: Bon anniversaire ! is the usual "happy birthday", and Joyeux anniversaire is what people sing, to the same tune as in English.
fact: Souffle les bougies ! means "Blow out the candles!"; une bougie is a candle and un gâteau d'anniversaire is a birthday cake.
fact: Years are said as whole numbers: 2026 is deux mille vingt-six; mille (thousand) never takes an s.
fact: Many French calendars give a saint's name for each day, and on your name's day people may say Bonne fête ! (happy name day); Saint Charles is on 4 November.
fact: Quelle est la date aujourd'hui ? means "What's the date today?"; a full answer is C'est le quatorze octobre, or with the day, C'est mardi quatorze octobre.
fact: J'ai eu dix ans hier ! means "I turned ten yesterday!"; learn it as a set birthday phrase.
fact: Bonne année ! ("bo-na-NAY") means Happy New Year and is said all through January the first time you see someone; New Year's Eve is la Saint-Sylvestre.
fact: Months take a small letter in French: le dix février, le vingt novembre.
fact: Slang here: "bro" means mate; "mint" (North of England) means great; "our kid" (Liverpool) means my brother; "grand" (Ireland) means fine or good; "eh" (Canada) asks you to agree; "proper job" (West Country) means great; "posh" means fancy.
exercise: How do you say the 1st of May? | le premier mai | le un mai | le premier de mai | le une mai
exercise: How do you say the 2nd of May? | le deux mai | le deuxième mai | le second mai | les deux mai
exercise: In France, which date is 05/03? | 5 March | 3 May | 5 May | 3 March
exercise: Ava asks her teacher about her birthday. Which question is polite for a teacher? | C'est quand, votre anniversaire ? | C'est quand, ton anniversaire, madame ? | C'est quand, ta anniversaire, madame ? | Quand c'est, tes anniversaire, madame ?
exercise: How do you say "My birthday is the 12th of June"? | Mon anniversaire, c'est le douze juin. | Ma anniversaire, c'est douze juin. | Mon birthday, c'est le douze juin. | Mon anniversaire, il est douze de juin.
exercise: What do French kids sing at a birthday party? | Joyeux anniversaire | Joyeux birthday | Bonne année | Bonne fête de Noël
exercise: What does Souffle les bougies ! mean? | Blow out the candles! | Wipe your nose! | Cut the cake now! | Sing louder, everyone!
exercise: What is une bougie? | a candle | a bogey | a cake | a balloon
exercise: How do you say 2026 in French? | deux mille vingt-six | vingt vingt-six | deux milles vingt-six | deux cent vingt-six
exercise: What does Bonne fête ! usually mean when a penpal writes it on 4 November to a boy called Charles? | Happy name day | Happy birthday, Charles | Have a nice holiday | Happy New Year, Charles
exercise: Isla says "le quatorze" when asked the date. What is missing? | the month: le quatorze octobre | the year: le quatorze deux mille | the word premier | nothing, it is complete
exercise: What does J'ai eu dix ans hier ! mean? | I turned ten yesterday! | I ate ten things yesterday! | I have ten more years left! | I'll be ten years old tomorrow!
exercise: When do French people say Bonne année ! ? | Through January, the first time they see someone | Only at midnight on 31 December, never after that | On their birthday | Only on 1 May
exercise: What is la Saint-Sylvestre? | New Year's Eve | New Year's Day, 1 January | a birthday cake | a saint's birthday party
exercise: How should Ruby write February in a French sentence? | février | Février | FEVRIER | fevrier
exercise: Which date is said with premier? | the 1st of the month | the last day of the month | every Monday | the 10th of the month
test: Emily asks, "Why's only the first one special?" What's the rule? | The 1st uses premier; all others use plain numbers | Every date uses premier, deuxième, troisième | Only the last day of a month is special | The 1st uses une because the month is feminine
test: Ryan's card arrives in March. He goes, "Bro, that's two months early." He had written 05/03 meaning May 3rd. What went wrong? | France writes day first, so his penpal read 5 March | The French post is always two months fast | France has no month called May | His penpal can't read numbers
test: The teacher tells Ava, "Use vous, cheeky." Why? | Ava said ton to a teacher; votre is polite | Ava should have spoken English | Ava said the wrong month | Teachers don't have birthdays in France
test: Harry says, "Mint, same song!" ("Mint" means great.) What do the French kids sing? | Joyeux anniversaire, to the same tune | Bonne année, to a different and much slower tune | Happy birthday in English | Frère Jacques, to a party tune
test: Lily asks, "Is she telling me off?" when her cousin shouts "Souffle les bougies !" What's the truth? | No, she's saying blow out the candles | Yes, she's saying stop eating the cake | Yes, she's saying wipe your nose | No, she's saying cut the cake
test: Leo writes "vingt vingt-six". His teacher says, "Yeah nah, French says two thousand twenty-six." ("Yeah nah" means no.) What's right? | deux mille vingt-six | deux milles vingt-six | vingt cent vingt-six | deux mille et vingt-six
test: Charlie says, "It's not my birthday, our kid," when Jules writes "Bonne fête !" on 4 November. ("Our kid" means my brother.) What happened? | Jules wished him a happy name day for Saint Charles | Jules got his birthday wrong | Jules was wishing him happy Christmas | Jules meant "have a good party tonight"
test: Isla's teacher says, "Grand, but which month?" ("Grand" means good.) Which is a full answer? | C'est le quatorze octobre. | C'est quatorze. | C'est le octobre quatorze. | C'est le quatorzième.
test: Ethan asks, "Is he boasting about his tea?" when a boy says "J'ai eu dix ans hier !" What did the boy mean? | He turned ten yesterday | He ate ten things yesterday | He has had ten teas | He's ten days old
test: Grace asks, "Eh, they keep saying Bonne année for weeks?" ("Eh" asks you to agree.) What's the custom? | It's said all January, the first time you meet someone that year | It's said only at midnight on New Year's Eve | It's said only to teachers | It's said only on 6 January
test: ★★★ Mia's birthday is le premier mars. Her brother's is exactly one week later. How do you say his birthday? | le huit mars | le sept mars | le premier mars | le neuf mars
test: ★★★ An American penpal writes 12/04 for her birthday, month first. How should a French friend say it? | le quatre décembre | le douze avril | le quatre avril | le premier décembre
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the expression of the first day of a month in French? | It is expressed by premier, whereas subsequent days are expressed by cardinal numbers | It is expressed by un, in the manner of all other days | It is expressed by the ordinal for every day of the month | It is omitted, the month alone being stated
exam: Identify the correct French rendering of the year 2026. | deux mille vingt-six | vingt vingt-six | deux milles vingt-six | deux cent vingt-six
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the French order of a written date. | The day precedes the month, after the British manner | The month precedes the day, after the American manner | The year precedes the day in all correspondence | The order is left to the preference of the writer
exam: It is given that a person states "J'ai eu dix ans hier". Determine the meaning of this statement. | The person attained the age of ten on the preceding day | The person consumed ten items on the preceding day | The person shall attain the age of ten on the following day | The person has resided in France for ten years
